    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "People can now name patrons from their own row, and each row shows the patrons and the backing. The `bin/e2e` acceptance test passes.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Adding a patron:** each row has a picker listing everyone on the sheet, plus an Add button. The server refuses the person themselves, someone already named, or someone not on the sheet. A refusal shows `person-patron-error` on the row and writes nothing. When it goes through, it saves and then writes `PATRON_ADDED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=<name> patron=<patron name>` to the audit file.\n- **Display:**\n  - `person-patrons` shows the patrons' names, sorted and joined with \", \".\n  - `person-backing` adds up the patrons' due-totals, skipping any that are n/a, and shows 0.00 when there are none.\n  - Backing reuses the existing due-total calculation, so holds and rates affect it the same way they affect due-totals.\n\n**Changes**\n- **Stored data:** new migration `V18__person_patron.sql` adds a `person_patron(person_id, patron_id)` table. `Person` holds the patron ids, and they come back in the person response as `patronIds`.\n- **Server:** new endpoint `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/patrons`. It follows the hold endpoint's steps: `ValidatePatron` \u2192 `LoadPerson` \u2192 `AddPatron` \u2192 `SavePerson` \u2192 `AuditPatronAdded` \u2192 `RespondWithPerson`.\n- **Front end:** new `features/people/patrons.slot.tsx`. I exported `useDueTotal` from `rates.slot.tsx` so the backing column can use it, and added `addPatron` and `patronIds` to `people.ts`.\n\n**Side effect:** adding a patron saves the person, which bumps their version number. If someone has that person open in the edit form at the same moment, their save will be refused as a conflict and they'll need to reload.",
